-- title:
--   q-expansion of T_ℓ on differentials in characteristic p
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ ($p$ prime), let $N \ge 1$, let $H' \le (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$, and let $\ell \ge 1$ be a prime with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\gcd(\ell, N) = 1$; assume $N \ne 0$ and $\ell \ne 0$ in $K$. Write $F =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC K (CohCarrier.GammaH N H')`, the $K$-subfield of $K((q))$ generated by the integral form ratios for the group $\Gamma_{H'}(N)$, obtained as the image in $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of $H'$ under $\Gamma_0(N) \to (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$. Two hypotheses are imposed: `HeckeBetaModLHDefined`, namely that substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$ carries every element of $F$ into the corresponding function field of $\Gamma_{H'}(N) \cap \Gamma_0(N\ell)$; and the existence of a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\Gamma_0(N)$ to the $K$-algebra automorphisms of $F$ satisfying `IsDiamondPullbackModL`, i.e. for all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(N)$, all weights $k$, all weight-$k$ modular forms $f, g, f_1, g_1$ on $\Gamma_{H'}(N)$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g, p_{f_1}, p_{g_1}$ such that $f_1 = f\vert_k\gamma$, $g_1 = g\vert_k\gamma$ and the series of $p_g$ is nonzero, every $x \in F$ whose Laurent series is $p_{f_1}/p_{g_1}$ has $\rho(\gamma)x$ with Laurent series $p_f/p_g$. Then for every Kähler differential $\omega \in \Omega[F/K]$ and every $n \in \mathbb{Z}$, the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion `diffQExp` (the lift of the derivation $q\,d/dq$) of `heckeDiffModLH K N H' ℓ ω` — the trace along the degeneracy map $q \mapsto q^\ell$ of the pull-back along the other degeneracy map — equals the coefficient at $n\ell$ of the $q$-expansion of $\omega$, plus $\ell$ times the coefficient at $n/\ell$ of the $q$-expansion of `diamondDiffModLH` at the unit of $\ell$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$ applied to $\omega$ when $\ell \mid n$, and plus $0$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the classical formula $a_n(T_\ell\omega) = a_{n\ell}(\omega) + \ell\, a_{n/\ell}(\langle\ell\rangle\omega)$ for the Hecke operator at a prime $\ell$ coprime to the level, transported to Kähler differentials of the function field of $X_{H'}(N)$ over an algebraically closed field of positive characteristic in which $N\ell$ is invertible, with the diamond operator realised as pull-back along the automorphism attached to a lift of $\ell^{-1}$ to $\Gamma_0(N)$. It feeds the identification of the $q$-expansion of $T_\ell$ acting on differentials with an explicit integral series on the two-cusp integral set.
